  "worked_solution": "Eight tulips cost $8T$ dollars, and four violets cost $4V$ dollars. Thus, the cost,  in dollars, of a bouquet is\n\n$$\n8T+4V.\n$$\n\nThomas' bill,  in dollars, comes to\n\n$$\n12(8T+4V).\n$$\n\nThis is $12$ times the cost of a single bouquet. Thus, the factor $12$ must be the total number of bouquets that Thomas purchased.",
